---
const marquee = ['Photography', 'Personal Branding', 'Short Film', 'Reels & Social', 'Creative Direction', 'Editorial', 'Portraiture'];
---
<section class="statement section" id="statement">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow reveal">( People connect with people )</p>
    <h2 class="statement__lead h-lg reveal">
      People remember <em>people and stories,</em> not logos. I make photo, film
      and social content built around <span class="u-red">you</span>.
    </h2>
    <div class="statement__meta">
      <p class="reveal muted">The Hague · Since 2024 · Working worldwide</p>
      <a href="#work" class="btn reveal">See the work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="marquee" data-marquee aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="marquee__track" data-marquee-track data-marquee-speed="55" data-marquee-slow="0">
      {[...marquee, ...marquee].map((w) => (
        <span class="marquee__item">{w}<i class="marquee__dot">✳</i></span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .statement {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    /* Slide up over the locked last Services card (Reels) instead of leaving a
       dead empty scroll. Opaque bg covers the dark card; higher z-index paints
       above it.

       margin-top is tuned so this block's top edge meets the fold EXACTLY when
       Reels locks, so it starts rising immediately — lock -> slide reads as ONE
       continuous motion with no frozen beat. Derivation: at the lock moment this
       block's top sits at  cardHeight + lock + pinnedTop - |margin|  down the
       page, and we want that to equal the viewport height (the fold):
         |margin| = cardHeight + lock - 100vh + pinnedTop
                  = 80vh + 70vh - 100vh + pinnedTop
                  = 50vh + pinnedTop
       where pinnedTop = Reels' sticky offset = Services' --svc-nav + 2*--peek
       = 4.5rem + 2*clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 6.5rem). A plain vh value can't do this:
       the beat is driven by pinnedTop (roughly fixed px), not by vh. The extra
       3vh (53 not 50) keeps the block a hair on-screen so there's zero risk of a
       1px gap. IF YOU CHANGE Services' .svc__card min-height (80vh), .svc__lock
       (70vh), --svc-nav (4.5rem) or --peek, update this calc to match. */
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    background: var(--bg);
    margin-top: calc(-53vh - 4.5rem - 2 * clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 6.5rem));
  }
  .statement__lead {
    max-width: 20ch;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.06;
  }
  .statement__lead em { font-style: italic; }
  .u-red { color: var(--red); }
  .statement__meta {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .marquee {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-block: 1.4rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .marquee__track {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .marquee__item {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
  }
  .marquee__dot { color: var(--red); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.4em; margin-left: 2.2rem; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    /* Matches Services: the sticky pin-stack is disabled on phones, so there's
       nothing to slide up over. Zero the negative overlap so this block just
       follows normally instead of yanking up over the cards (which jumped). */
    .statement { margin-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
